## Architecture Boundaries

### Allowed

- Read and write files in `src/features/`, `src/components/`, `src/utils/`
- Create new files following existing directory structure
- Run tests and lint commands

### Read-Only (do not modify)

- `src/payment/` — 支付核心模块
- `src/auth/` — 认证模块
- `config/` — 配置文件

### Forbidden

- `.env*` — 环境变量，禁止访问
- `migrations/` — 数据库迁移，禁止创建或修改
- Do not install new dependencies without confirmation
- Do not modify CI/CD configuration files

## Verification Rules (Chapter 5)

<!--
  这些规则来自第 5 章 5.9 的验证纪律
  Anthropic 在 10 万行 C 代码项目中验证了"不许改测试"规则的必要性
-->

1. NEVER delete or modify existing test cases unless the requirement itself changed
2. When tests fail, fix the source code, NOT the tests
3. New features MUST include tests
4. All code must compile/run successfully
5. All existing tests must pass
6. Do not claim "done" without providing verification output (test results, screenshots, logs)

## Coding Constraints (Chapter 3)

<!--
  每条约束来自真实踩坑，给理由让 AI 遇到边界场景时能自己判断
-->

Forbidden patterns:
- No `any` type in TypeScript (fix the type properly)
- No hardcoded URLs, ports, API keys, or secrets
- No `console.log` in committed code (use project logger)
- No `// @ts-ignore` or `// @ts-expect-error`
- No direct DOM manipulation in framework components
- No `eval()` or `new Function()`

Required patterns:
- All API calls go through the API layer, not directly in components
- Error handling on every external call (API, DB, file I/O)
- Input validation on all user-facing endpoints

## Change Scope Control (Chapter 6)

<!--
  校准时最烦人的模式：你让 AI 改 A，它"顺手"改了 B 和 C（第 6 章 6.2）
-->

- Only modify files directly related to the current task
- Do not "improve" or refactor code you were not asked to touch
- Do not change function signatures in other modules unless explicitly requested
- If a refactor is needed, ask first before making changes

## Context Tips (Chapter 4)

<!--
  上下文工程原则：少即是多，给 AI 最小有效上下文
-->

- When unsure about project conventions, read existing code in the same directory first
- Reference existing files for style: "follow the pattern in [file]"
- For data formats, look at existing API response examples in `docs/` or test fixtures
- If you need information not available in the codebase, ask rather than guess

## Security (Chapter 5)

- Parameterized queries only, no string concatenation for SQL
- No `innerHTML` with user input (XSS risk)
- No `shell=True` with user-provided input (command injection risk)
- No `verify=False` for SSL (man-in-the-middle risk)
- Secrets in environment variables, never in code
- Authentication required on all API routes unless explicitly public
